{title: 054 - O Gladsome Light}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #054 • PHOS HILARON • 6.6.8.6.6.7}
{lyricist: Robert S. Bridges}
{composer: James Bingham}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 54}
{meta: tune PHOS HILARON}
{meta: meter 6.6.8.6.6.7}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]O gladsome [Bb]light, [Am]O [F]grace
[Dm]Of God [C]the Father's [Dm]face,
[C/G]The eternal splendor [Am]wearing;
[Dm]Celestial, [F]holy, blest,
[Gm]Our [F]Savior, Jesus Christ,
[Dm]Joyful [F]in Thine [Am]appearing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Now e'er day [Bb]fadeth [F]quite,
[Dm]We see [C]the ev'ning [Dm]light,
[C/G]Our [Dm]wonted [Gm]hymn [C]ourpouring;
[Dm]Father [F]of might unknown,
[Gm]Thee [F]His [C]incarnate [F]Son,
[Dm]And Holy [F]Spirit [Am]adoring.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]To Thee of [Bb]right [Am]belongs
[Dm]All praise [C]of holy [Dm]songs,
[C/G]O [Dm]Son [F]of [Gm]God, [C]life [Am]giver;
[Dm]Thee therefore, [F]O most high,
[Gm]The [F]world [C]doth [F/A]glorify
[Dm]And shall [F]exalt [Am]for ever.
{end_of_verse}
